  "id": "lineup",
  "term": "lineup",
  "definition": "A lineup is an eyewitness identification procedure in which a suspect is shown together with other known-innocent people, and the witness is asked whether any of them is the person who committed the crime. In research and legal contexts, lineups may be described as target-present when the suspect is guilty or target-absent when the suspect is innocent.",
